.EX
#define KNR_STYLE
.EE
.PP
Defined if the compiler is not using ANSI C syntax (i.e., K&R / pre\-C89
mode).
.PP
Indicates that the compiler lacks support for standard function
prototypes and modern type qualifiers.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS void
.IP
.EX
#define void
.EE
.PP
Defined as \f[CR]char\f[R] for K&R compilers that do not support the
\f[CR]void\f[R] keyword.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS const
.IP
